{
  "id": "lolin-d32-pro",
  "name": "LOLIN D32 Pro",
  "baseChip": "esp32wrover",
  "pcb": "black",
  "notes": [
    "LOLIN (WEMOS) D32 Pro v2.0.0: 65 x 25.4 mm ESP32-WROVER (16 MB flash / 8 MB PSRAM current, 4 MB flash early runs) with a CH340C bridge, micro-USB, LiPo charging (PH-2 + TP4054), a microSD (TF) slot, and SH1.0 ports for a TFT (10-pin) and I2C (4-pin). Auto-flash circuit onboard - no BOOT button needed.",
    "GPIO16/17 never reach the headers (the WROVER's PSRAM uses them; the pads are silkscreened NC). GPIO35 is not broken out either - it reads the battery through a 100k/100k divider (voltage = reading x 2).",
    "The microSD and TFT ports reserve GPIO4 (TF_CS), 14 (TFT_CS), 27 (DC), 33 (RST), 32 (backlight) and 12 (touch CS), all sharing the VSPI bus on GPIO18/19/23."
  ],
